  "body": "## Summary\n\nWhen portable-project export or import hits a size or complexity guard, the Project menu previously showed only the raw error. It now adds specific recovery guidance beside Import/Export, links to the unchanged format limits, and explains browser-local preservation, separately downloaded reports, and smaller projects for future work. Unknown errors keep their original message.\n\nValidate imports before clearing the active result context so rejected files preserve the current RF evidence. Keep the menu scrollable within the viewport when recovery help is visible.\n\n## Linked issue\n\nCloses #77.\n\n## Affected surfaces\n\nProject menu, rejected-import result handling, frontend interaction and workflow tests, portable-format documentation, changelog, and generated reference pages.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] `cd frontend-react && npm run lint` passed.\n- [x] `cd frontend-react && npm test` passed: 477 tests across 73 files, including existing project-file reliability tests and deterministic injected import/export failures.\n- [x] `cd frontend-react && npm run build` passed.\n- [x] `cd frontend-react && npm run test:e2e -- e2e/workspace.spec.js e2e/persistence-reliability.spec.js -g 'project budget recovery preserves|six-Cell' --workers=2` passed: 29 tests, 3 existing skips.\n- [x] Final `npm run test:e2e -- e2e/workspace.spec.js -g 'project budget recovery preserves' --workers=2` passed at all four viewport sizes, including actual Markdown download, retained report download, PDF/Print output, and New/project switching without RF retries.\n- [x] Rebuilt references with pinned Pandoc 3.10; `python docs/validate_docs.py`, `python docs/validate_claims.py`, `python3 scripts/versioning.py check`, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- [x] Backend and adapter checks skipped locally because their code is unchanged.\n\nFrontend commands used the bundled Node 24 runtime because the system Node installation is missing a shared library. Documentation commands used the existing isolated environment with pinned dependencies.\n\n## Screenshots (UI changes only)\n\nRecovery guidance at desktop and mobile widths:\n\n<img width=\"280\" alt=\"Desktop Project menu showing budget recovery guidance\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Berk-Unsal/atom/bfab6dd8adbf6544f52fd6c306d3dc122d79bc32/docs/assets/project-file-recovery/desktop-1440.png\">\n<img width=\"280\" alt=\"Mobile Project menu showing budget recovery guidance\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Berk-Unsal/atom/bfab6dd8adbf6544f52fd6c306d3dc122d79bc32/docs/assets/project-file-recovery/mobile-390.png\">\n\n## Boundary notes (RF / scope / persistence / compatibility changes)\n\nNo guard increases, schema changes, new archive/export mode, scientific-data trimming, automatic deletion, or RF retries. Reports are explicitly described as separate documents rather than full editable backups. Rejected-import handling preserves the active project's current result context. Maintainer review is required for this persistence failure-path change.\n\n## Changelog\n\nRecorded under Unreleased in `CHANGELOG.md`; updated portable-format recovery documentation and regenerated reference pages/search index.\n",
